[T034] Error: `toString` cannot declare `throws`: rendering a value has to be infallible
   ╭─[ a_to_string_override_cannot_declare_throws.bras:6:37 ]
   │
 6 │   def toString(self): string throws Boom
   │                                     ──┬─  
   │                                       ╰─── remove this contract
   │ 
   │ Note 1: `toString` is reached from `puts`, string interpolation, and every container, `Option`, tuple, and enum that renders its elements, as well as from error reporting itself — a failure there has nowhere left to be reported
   │ 
   │ Note 2: handle the failure inside `toString` with a `catch` and render a fallback, or move the fallible work to a method with another name
